               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 61-year-old male, who presented on 23rd March 1967 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically consistent with acute appendicitis. On admission, physical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point with guarding. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasonography supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. Given the clinical picture, the patient underwent a laparoscopic appendectomy without intraoperative complications. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound care was provided, pain was managed adequately with analgesics, and the patient was mobilised early. He was discharged home on 26th March 1967 in good general condition. Please ensure appropriate follow-up and wound inspection. Do not hesitate to contact me should any concerns arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
